quency key — thirty seconds of the before — and watched their faces change. They stood aside. Some revolutions are just remembering, together."}, {'n': 4, 'title': 'The Remembering', 'text': "Iris Novak and the runner Pax were in the tower when the door blew. The ex-enforcer held the stairs long enough. Long enough for what? For the footage to loop. For the memory to root. For the Consortium's lie to die on every screen at once.\n\nWhat happened in the next hour, historians argue about. What Iris Novak remembers: silence, then a sound like a held breath released, then the streets filling with people who had remembered they were people.\n\na frequency key burned out in the broadcast — one use, that was the price. Iris Novak held the dead chip and didn't mourn it. Seeds die to grow. That was the whole point."}, {'n': 5, 'title': 'After the Static', 'text': "Rebuilding the Outer Rings was harder than freeing it. Iris Novak organized food lines with the same care once used for heists. the runner Pax taught kids to code on salvaged terminals. The medic ran a clinic. The runner ran messages of hope.\n\nThere were trials. the Consortium's people faced justice — real justice, not the Algorithm's kind, with evidence and mercy both. Some were guilty. Some were just afraid. Iris Novak learned the difference matters.\n\nAnd when the new council asked Iris Novak to lead, Iris Novak laughed and went back to the food lines. Leaders, Iris Novak had learned, are just people who show up. Iris Novak shows up."}, {'n': 6, 'title': 'The Habit of Freedom', 'text': "the runner Pax runs the network now — the real one, the open one, the one that belongs to everyone. The neon is quieter. The neon is warmer. It turns out freedom has a sound, and it's laughter.\n\nYears later, the Outer Rings has gardens on the roofs and children who've never seen a drone. They learn the story of a frequency key in school, and Iris Novak always winces at the statue. 'I just carried it,' Iris Novak protests. Nobody believes that anymore.\n\nAnd somewhere, in a gutter where drones don't look, someone is finding something warm that shouldn't be warm. It starts again. It always starts again. That's the best part."}]}

def word_count():
    return sum(len(c["text"].split()) for c in BOOK["chapters"])

def print_book(ch=None):
    print("=" * 64)
    print(BOOK["title"].upper(), "\nby", BOOK["author"], "-", BOOK["genre"])
    print("=" * 64)
    for c in BOOK["chapters"]:
        if ch and c["n"] != ch:
            continue
        print("\n\nCHAPTER %d: %s\n%s" % (c["n"], c["title"], "-" * 40))
        print(c["text"])
    print("\n[%d words, %d chapters — complete]" % (word_count(), len(BOOK["chapters"])))

def search(word):
    w = word.lower()
    for c in BOOK["chapters"]:
        for i, para in enumerate(c["text"].split("\n\n")):
            if w in para.lower():
                print("[ch %d, para %d] %s..." % (c["n"], i + 1, para[:160].replace("\n", " ")))

def write_html(path="book.html"):
    parts = ["<html><head><meta charset='utf-8'><title>%s</title></head><body>" % _h.escape(BOOK["title"])]
    parts.append("<h1>%s</h1><p><i>by %s — %s</i></p>" % (_h.escape(BOOK["title"]), _h.escape(BOOK["author"]), _h.escape(BOOK["genre"])))
    for c in BOOK["chapters"]:
        parts.append("<h2>Chapter %d: %s</h2>" % (c["n"], _h.escape(c["title"])))
        for para in c["text"].split("\n\n"):
            parts.append("<p>%s</p>" % _h.escape(para))
    parts.append("</body></html>")
    open(path, "w").write("\n".join(parts))
    print("wrote", path)

if __name__ == "__main__":
    a = sys.argv[1:]
    if a and a[0] == "html":
        write_html()
    elif len(a) >= 2 and a[0] == "search":
        search(a[1])
    elif a and a[0].isdigit():
        print_book(int(a[0]))
    else:
        print_book()

